@host = http://localhost:5119
@email = alice@example.com
@password = Password123

### Register (then open http://localhost:8025 to read the confirmation email)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Login — 403 until the email is confirmed, then 200 with a token
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Who am I (uses the token from the login request above)
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Wrong password → 401
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "nope"
}

###
GET {{host}}/about.json

###
GET {{host}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

###
GET {{host}}/widgets
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Run a widget once without creating an instance
GET {{host}}/widgets/weather.current/preview?city=Lille
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

###
GET {{host}}/widgets/weather.forecast/preview?city=Tokyo&days=3&unit=fahrenheit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Services the account has access to (subscribed = usable now)
GET {{host}}/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Subscribe to a service whose auth kind is apiKey (none shipped yet; GitHub uses OAuth)
POST {{host}}/subscriptions/some-service
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "apiKey": "secret-key"
}

### Unsubscribe
DELETE {{host}}/subscriptions/some-service
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### The dashboard: this user's widget instances
GET {{host}}/widget-instances
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Add a widget to the dashboard
# @name instance
POST {{host}}/widget-instances
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "widgetKey": "weather.current",
  "config": { "city": "Lille", "unit": "celsius" },
  "refreshRateSeconds": 900,
  "position": { "x": 0, "y": 0, "width": 2, "height": 2 }
}

### A second instance of the same widget, another city
POST {{host}}/widget-instances
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "widgetKey": "weather.forecast",
  "config": { "city": "Tokyo", "days": 5, "unit": "celsius" },
  "refreshRateSeconds": 3600
}

### Reconfigure it (config + refresh rate)
PUT {{host}}/widget-instances/{{instance.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "config": { "city": "Paris" },
  "refreshRateSeconds": 600
}

### Move or resize it
PATCH {{host}}/widget-instances/{{instance.response.body.$.id}}/position
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "x": 2, "y": 1, "width": 3, "height": 2 }

### Remove it from the dashboard
DELETE {{host}}/widget-instances/{{instance.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Duolingo: public learning profile
GET {{host}}/widgets/duolingo.profile/preview?username=test
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Duolingo: the course currently being learnt
GET {{host}}/widgets/duolingo.course/preview?username=test
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Duolingo: another course of the same user
GET {{host}}/widgets/duolingo.course/preview?username=test&language=ja
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### The whole dashboard's data in one call (what the grid polls)
GET {{host}}/widget-instances/data
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### One widget's latest refresh
GET {{host}}/widget-instances/{{instance.response.body.$.id}}/data
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
